WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
What lives in a patch of plain grass?

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.380
Give your child ten minutes to look closely and test a guess.

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.640
A string square gives you a place to start.

4
00:00:12.717 --> 00:00:15.177
Here is what your child practices today.

5
00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:20.637
They practice slowing down, looking closely, and testing a guess with a count.

6
00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:24.517
They also sort living parts from nonliving parts.

7
00:00:25.757 --> 00:00:27.357
They discover one big idea.

8
00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:33.837
Every animal needs a habitat that supplies food, water, air, shelter, and space.

9
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.230
Stay within arm's reach the whole time.

10
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.810
Choose dry ground away from roads and water.

11
00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.570
Check for glass, sharp litter, and ant mounds.

12
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.690
Keep pebbles, small pegs, and other small objects away from children under four.

13
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.450
Call nine one one if choking.

14
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.540
Setup uses simple items.

15
00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.200
Bring about four and a half meters of string, four sticks, a pencil, and paper.

16
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.940
Add a magnifying glass if you have one, plus garden gloves for rolling a log.

17
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.320
Push the four sticks about one meter apart and wrap the string around them.

18
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:18.883
Before you look, ask your child, “How many animals do you think we will find in our

19
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:20.583
square?” Write down the guess.

20
00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:23.843
Then spend ten minutes looking closely.

21
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:29.503
Part the grass gently with a pencil, and count each animal you see inside the

22
00:01:29.503 --> 00:01:30.503
string.

23
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:33.113
Now picture that square before you kneel.

24
00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.193
From up here, it looks like plain grass.

25
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:41.113
What do you predict you will see moving in the square once you part the grass?

26
00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:49.843
Here, parting the grass reveals an ant and a spider.

27
00:01:51.223 --> 00:01:53.783
Your square may look different with the season and weather.

28
00:01:55.263 --> 00:01:56.603
Grass itself is alive, too.

29
00:01:57.943 --> 00:02:00.983
When you finish looking, compare your count with your child’s guess.

30
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:05.143
Next, help your child sort the square into two lists.

31
00:02:06.463 --> 00:02:11.483
List living things like grass and ants, and nonliving things like soil, rocks, and

32
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:14.683
sunlight. Then pick one animal together.

33
00:02:16.123 --> 00:02:17.443
Ask, Where does this ant eat?

34
00:02:18.723 --> 00:02:19.883
Where could it find water?

35
00:02:21.123 --> 00:02:23.003
Together, trace its shelter and space.

36
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:25.423
You can skip the log.

37
00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:30.883
If you look under one, have your child stand back while you put on garden gloves.

38
00:02:32.163 --> 00:02:35.363
Choose a light log and roll it toward you without lifting it.

39
00:02:36.463 --> 00:02:39.283
Look underneath, then gently roll it back into place.

40
00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:42.923
Never put hands or feet where you cannot see.

41
00:02:44.343 --> 00:02:45.643
Step back if you see a snake.

42
00:02:46.903 --> 00:02:48.703
Watch animals where they are.

43
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:50.683
Keep your hands off them.

44
00:02:51.803 --> 00:02:54.243
Never taste plants, berries, or mushrooms.

45
00:02:55.603 --> 00:02:57.283
Handle any glass lens yourself.

46
00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:01.583
Keep every magnifying glass pointed away from the sun.

47
00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.387
Pull up the sticks and string, and put back any leaves you moved.

48
00:03:07.607 --> 00:03:10.987
Wash hands with soap and water and check for ticks afterward.

49
00:03:12.347 --> 00:03:14.007
Think back to the animal you watched.

50
00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:17.847
Its habitat is the place it finds what it needs.
